---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Dustbound and dustbound.app handle your data — local-first Android app, no website analytics, and what Formspree receives from the interest signup."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 prose-invert" data-testid="privacy-page">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-ink">Dustbound Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 10 August 2026</p>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-3 text-muted" data-testid="privacy-intro">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong class="text-ink">Ingenium Software Engineering</strong>
        (“we”, “us”, or “Ingenium”) handles information in connection with the mobile application
        <strong class="text-ink">Dustbound</strong> (Android package <code class="text-ink">dev.ingeniumsoftware.dustbound</code>)
        and the website at <a href="https://dustbound.app/">https://dustbound.app/</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dustbound is a local-first companion checklist for tracking Sprite collectible progress. It is an unofficial product.
        Dustbound is not affiliated with, endorsed by, supported by, or connected to Epic Games, Inc., and it does not contain any Fortnite materials.
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev">privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Canonical URL: <a href="https://dustbound.app/privacy/">https://dustbound.app/privacy/</a>.
        See also our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-muted" data-testid="privacy-app">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">App</h2>
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Summary</h3>
      <p>
        Dustbound stores your checklist progress and preferences on your device only. We do not create user accounts,
        do not upload your progress to our servers, and do not use analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting SDKs.
        The app may download publicly available catalog and events data over the internet so checklists stay up to date.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Information stored on your device</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Checklist progress</strong> — which collectibles you have marked as Collected or Mastered.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Preferences</strong> — optional event timezone override and local Event notification settings.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Content caches</strong> — copies of public catalog and events data used offline or between refreshes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This on-device data is not transmitted to Ingenium. If Android Backup is enabled, the operating system may include
        app data in device backups according to your system settings.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Network access and permissions</h3>
      <p>
        Dustbound may use network access to download public catalog and events JSON feeds over HTTPS from hosting provided
        via GitHub Pages. These requests do not include your checklist progress. Hosting providers may incidentally receive
        technical information such as IP address and User-Agent. Ingenium does not operate a separate analytics backend for Dustbound.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you enable Event reminders, Dustbound requests notification permission so it can schedule local reminders.
        Reminder content stays on device; we do not send push notifications from Ingenium servers.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Information we do not collect</h3>
      <p>
        Dustbound does not require accounts, sync progress to Ingenium, include advertising/analytics/crash SDKs,
        or collect precise location, contacts, photos, microphone audio, SMS, call logs, or advertising identifiers for our use.
        Purchases of the paid app are handled by Google Play under Google’s policies.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Sharing, security, retention</h3>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal or sensitive user data. Limited third-party involvement includes GitHub Pages (public feeds)
        and Google Play (distribution and paid download). Checklist progress stays in the app’s private on-device storage.
        Network fetches use HTTPS. On-device data is retained until you clear app data or uninstall Dustbound.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Children</h3>
      <p>Dustbound is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through the app.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-muted" data-testid="privacy-website">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Website</h2>
      <p>
        The Dustbound marketing website at dustbound.app may collect <strong class="text-ink">email addresses only</strong>
        when you use the interest signup form, for the purpose of notifying you about early release / launch of the Dustbound app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Submissions are processed by <strong class="text-ink">Formspree</strong> on our behalf. See
        <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree’s Privacy Policy</a>.
        We retain interest emails only for that notification purpose, then delete or stop using them for it.
        To request deletion, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev">privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Formspree Free plans may keep dashboard submission history for a limited window; we may export addresses as needed
        to fulfil the notification purpose before that window ends.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website does not set first-party cookies and does not use analytics. See the
        <a href="/cookies/">Cookie policy</a> for details. GitHub Pages (and any CDN in front of it) may process
        standard connection/technical data when serving the site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-3 text-muted">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.
        The current version remains at <a href="https://dustbound.app/privacy/">https://dustbound.app/privacy/</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
